      "synopsis": "Haydée tells Albert how Fernand surrendered Ali Pasha, seized treasure, and sold Vasiliki and her daughter. Within Haydée’s recollection, Fernand surrenders Ali Pasha’s stronghold after promising loyal service. The remembered journey ends in the Constantinople slave market, where Haydée and Vasiliki are sold after Yanina’s fall. The document records that Fernand sold Haydée and Vasiliki after Ali Pasha’s fall.",
