      "number": 116,
      "title": "The Pardon",
      "synopsis": "At the edge of starvation, Danglars repents; Monte Cristo reveals himself, leaves him fifty thousand francs, and releases him. After costly hunger has consumed nearly everything, Danglars clutches the final reserve and asks merely to live.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
    },
    {
      "worldId": "count-of-monte-cristo-world",
      "createdAt": 1786291200000,
      "updatedAt": 1786291200000,
      "id": "count-of-monte-cristo-chapter-117",
      "timelineId": "count-of-monte-cristo-timeline-main",
      "number": 117,
      "title": "The Fifth of October",
      "synopsis": "On 5 October at Monte Cristo, Valentine is restored to Maximilien and Haydée’s love gives Edmond permission to imagine a future beyond judgment. Before the Count departs, Valentine steps from concealment and ends Maximilien’s belief that hope was empty.",
      "notes": "",
      "wordGoal": null
    }
  ],
